                <pb facs="0291" n="192" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg192"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">835.6363/452: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Cox</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-28T17:00:00-04:00">August 28, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 7 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>177. My 173, August 24, noon. Standard Oil Company today informs me that latest
                    proposal of commission to the private companies <pb facs="0292" n="193"
                        xml:id="pg193"/> provides for signing a temporary agreement discontinuing
                    special rebates and discounts pending the signature of a marketing arrangement
                    on September 20. All companies execpt Shell-Mex and Standard, I am informed,
                    have signed this agreement, Standard insisting no time limit be set in order to
                    permit Vice President Harden to come from London for discussion.</p>
                <p>Standard understands that marketing arrangement, to constitute regulations under
                    executive decree of July 20, will be drafted shortly by a committee including
                    Standard Oil Company representative and will be along lines of proscriptive
                    rules summarized in despatch 1297 of August 7.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Cox</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
